{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/116314-prometheans-are-what-exactly","id":116314,"title":"Prometheans are....what exactly?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Promethean: The Created"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-04-19T20:43:34-07:00","id":116314,"title":"Prometheans are....what exactly?","content":"More to the point: what do they detect as?<br /> <br /> I'm about to enter a cross-over game where I'm playing a promethean, but then players started to ask me things like &quot;does a promethean pings a Death Sight spell?&quot; &quot;What is the age a promethean detects as?&quot; or &quot;what is the 48 prime number excluding all those containing the number 3&quot; (this has nothing to do with the question though)<br /> <br /> So I guess my real question is: what does the Promethean detects as? Dead? Alive? Young? Old? Does it trigger Forces sight? Death Sight? Prime Sight?<br /> <br /> Thank you,<br /> Magnum Opus","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Useless-Post Prana<br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Cost: 2</span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">m; </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mins: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Linguistics 1, Essence 1 </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Type: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Simple</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Keywords: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mute</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Duration: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Instant</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Prerequisite Charms: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Ten-Characters Methodology</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2589-magnum-opus","name":"Magnum Opus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2589_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"821"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-19T23:35:08-07:00","id":116360,"title":"","content":"Book of the Dead has some mechanics for Prometheans registering as alive, dead, or something else when checked for such by magic powers. Might be worth a look.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-20T06:24:04-07:00","id":116470,"title":"","content":"Prime Sight sees the strange nature of a Promethean almost immediately. Death Sight and Life Sight can both uncover its nature to some extent. Other sights might detect other peculiarities, like their affinity for electricity with Forces sight. What Time Sight sees would likely greatly depend on Lineage, with a Frankenstein potentially looking like the mish mash he/she is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-20T10:12:52-07:00","id":116567,"title":"","content":"All the major splats, essentially, are oddities on some level. Mummies, for example, register strangely with Death Sight.<br /> <br /> Question: &quot;Are Mummies alive or dead?&quot; Answer: &quot;Yes&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-21T04:39:12-07:00","id":116882,"title":"","content":"Prometheans and Mummys are very special cases (even if the whole &quot;soul&quot; is very mysterious even in the case of mortals) because they involve forces which are by definition outside the Supernal Magic. (Divine Fire and magic of &quot;death&quot; linked to the Lower Depths)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/343-suleri-drals","name":"Suleri Drals","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar343_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"244"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-21T08:04:01-07:00","id":116945,"title":"","content":"Don't certain arcana have effects on <i>Inferno</i> demons, which are from the Lower Depths? If so, might not Death still affect Mummies?<br /> <br /> Prometheans, though, I have no idea. To me, they have their origins in the Depths, too, and the Divine Fire pulled them to our reality like a fisherman pulling a fish from the deep. I don't think Death would have the same effects on the Created, though","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-21T09:05:33-07:00","id":116978,"title":"","content":"Creatures of the Lower Depths are <b><i>semi</i></b>-real; they are still partly defined by patterns and scannable with arcanas; but they are also partially &quot;indefinite&quot;; something missing but which is nevertheless what defines the most them; making them as strange as the beings of the Abyss because they are mostly what they are not. Sometimes a demon is defined as a spirit; sometimes not; but there was always something missing. (Some demons have a mind well defined but have no matter analyzable by arcanas, ect ...)<br /> Very deeply; there are things that are complety shaped ; no arcanum, no supernal symbol; beings wich who are not but can still eat.<br /> <br /> Arcana of Death can still partially define the mummies; but there is something else.<br /> <br /> If a mage reads the soul of a mummy; he will see that he is both alive, undead, and something opaque and impenetrable for the arcanas.<br /> <br /> Promies are also composed of arcanas and supernal models : their bodies, affinitys with Forces,ect......but the divine fire can only be very roughly seen by a high level of Mind and Prime. (And it is rather indirect; like seeing only the deformations of the structure of the astral and the magic caused by the Divine Fire.)<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":343,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/343-suleri-drals","user":"Suleri Drals","date":". 04-21-2014, 12:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/343-suleri-drals","name":"Suleri Drals","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar343_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"244"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-23T12:00:24-07:00","id":118035,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnum Opus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/116314-prometheans-are-what-exactly#post116314\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm about to enter a cross-over game where I'm playing a promethean, but then players started to ask me things like &quot;does a promethean pings a Death Sight spell?&quot; &quot;What is the age a promethean detects as?&quot; or &quot;what is the 48 prime number excluding all those containing the number 3&quot; (this has nothing to do with the question though)<br /> <br /> So I guess my real question is: what does the Promethean detects as? Dead? Alive? Young? Old? Does it trigger Forces sight? Death Sight? Prime Sight?<br /> <br /> Thank you,<br /> Magnum Opus</div> </div> </div> </div> As with all things crossover, I tend to suggest you ignore individual rules, and go with what makes sense for your game. Because, depending on what writer is about, what references you look up, Prometheans could be undead, alive, differently alive, or any number of other things. Go with what makes most sense to you, because then its easier for you to be more consistent. If you want a Promethean to be a variant zombie, then its easiest to run it that way. If you want them to be a living creature (ITS ALIVEEEEEE!!!!) then go with that. Something crazy that breaks the rules? Go for it<br /> <br /> And, honestly... I would just say, &quot;why don't you have your mage find out in game?&quot; This is exactly the kind of thing that mages do, investigate mysteries. Its not nearly as much fun if they gets all the answers OOC.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-26T07:25:39-07:00","id":119727,"title":"","content":"Thanks MCN, I'll probably let the Mage and the Geist figure out what I may be during gameplay. It'll be funny because I don't really know what I am to start with.<br /> <br /> I may try and get my hands on a copy of the Book of the Dead too, in order to see what they have to say about us Prometheans.<br /> <br /> Thanks!<br /> - Magnum Opus","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Useless-Post Prana<br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Cost: 2</span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">m; </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mins: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Linguistics 1, Essence 1 </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Type: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Simple</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Keywords: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mute</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Duration: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Instant</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Prerequisite Charms: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Ten-Characters Methodology</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2589-magnum-opus","name":"Magnum Opus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2589_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"821"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-27T19:32:14-07:00","id":120669,"title":"","content":"&quot;what is the 48 prime number excluding all those containing the number 3&quot; <br /> <br /> 479?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2030-baboonking","name":"baboonking","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2030_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-28T22:19:10-07:00","id":121499,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>baboonking</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/116314-prometheans-are-what-exactly?p=120669#post120669\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;what is the 48 prime number excluding all those containing the number 3&quot;<br /> <br /> 479?</div> </div> </div> </div>491, actually. :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-29T18:50:38-07:00","id":122133,"title":"","content":"This is a great question as Prometheans are tough to identify exactly... Especially since part of their personal quests is to become human - at what point does a promethean detect as alive? Are they really dead since they have azoth and pyros? Also, not all prometheans were once dead... the unfleshed can't really be undead.<br /> <br /> Looking at other posts on this thread, I have to agree that it is up to your individual ST's to figure out this works as for each chronicle it will be different.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2826-mikerand","name":"mikerand","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2826_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-01T20:00:55-07:00","id":123582,"title":"","content":"I don't agree that Divine Fire is linked to anything that's easy to point at, Lower Depths or arcana or anything else defined by the other denizens of the World of Darkness. That's not to say such notions are <i>WRONG</i>, but I think that any labels being seen as The Truth\u2122 robs that power of much of its, well... POWER, on a story level anyway.<br /> <br /> One of the <b>Promethean: the Created</b> supplements (can't recall which, <i>Saturnine Night</i> maybe?) says that the very nature of Divine Fire is based on very specific measures, but it only flares in moments of impossible desperation. It presents a notion that once a demiurge has succeeded in the act of creation, once he KNOWS it can be done, that spark won't ever flare the same way again...<br /> <br /> So, in terms of the topic at hand, I feel it's perfectly possible that one of the Created could look different to a vampire, to a mage, to a changeling, and none of those beings' respective powers would work as expected on one of the Created. Further, as my reading of <i>Mortal Remains</i> for <b>Hunter: the Vigil</b> suggests, different Lineages could all appear different to whatever supernatural senses are focused upon them. A mage looking at a throng of prommies might not immediately know that the Wretched, Orsirian and Galateid were all of single type.<br /> <br /> I love how properly <i>odd</i> <b>Promethean</b> is in the World of Darkness, and any crossover that includes this line would, for my game at least, play up the unknowable nature of those creatures.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>B.I.G. Bird spreads the word: Anybody with a heart votes love<br /> <a href=\"https://absintheandthorns.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">https://absintheandthorns.obsidianportal.com/</a></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/409-phaolan","name":"Phaolan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar409_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"478"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-01T20:38:41-07:00","id":123591,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Phaolan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/116314-prometheans-are-what-exactly?p=123582#post123582\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't agree that Divine Fire is linked to anything that's easy to point at, Lower Depths or arcana or anything else defined by the other denizens of the World of Darkness.</div> </div> </div> </div>While I disagree with the theory that the Fire is necessarily from the Depths, I must point out that the Lower Depths are easy to point at in the sense that it's easy to point at things that are on the ground. It's an umbrella category for &quot;places that aren't entirely real, aren't well-understood, and may or may not want to eat and/or mutate us.&quot;<br /> <br /> Remember Flux.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-05T10:59:56-07:00","id":125965,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Phaolan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/116314-prometheans-are-what-exactly?p=123582#post123582\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I love how properly <i>odd</i> <b>Promethean</b> is in the World of Darkness, and any crossover that includes this line would, for my game at least, play up the unknowable nature of those creatures.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is how it should be. If there were a Chronicle GMC-update book for the game the only major revision I would want is to make each individual Promethean even more unique. I don't necessarily want to ditch lineages, but I'd love <i>Promethean</i>'s character creation process to be more free-form, to really drive home that they are Weird in a world of weirdness. I never want to see them tied to the Lower Depths in a published book, and I fancy the idea in my head-canon, but really they need to be as alien and foreign as possible","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-09T22:53:53-07:00","id":129640,"title":"","content":"Part of what I like about Promethean is that - you are pretty &quot;weird&quot; and foreign out the gate.<br /> All the added stuff in &quot;Strange Alchemies,&quot; &quot;Magnum Opus&quot; and &quot;Saturnine Night&quot; lets the Storyteller throw <i>even more weird</i> at the Promethean PCs. In a crossover game? It basically lets you play tulpa and robots.<br /> It's out there, man.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1S8EuNtxeJKwq4sKVVPe16_N0ylIashKpgfCCuA1UOM8/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Promethean Homebrew.</a><br /> <br /> Yes, I made it the same way as a Promethean. No, the authorities haven't found me yet.","edited":{"userid":685,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/685-ben-quo","user":"Ben Quo","date":". 05-10-2014, 11:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/685-ben-quo","name":"Ben Quo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar685_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-20T05:41:14-07:00","id":143335,"title":"","content":"I've always been of the mind that to the general WOD population, and to the Mages especially, the Prometheans always read as &quot;other&quot;. They don't come across completely as alive or dead, as real or not real, or as this or that. I always toyed with the idea that (and I know this would be totally abhorrent to most Mage players) the reason Supernal magics can't replicate or detect Prometheans and Divine Fire is because there is no Supernal version of them. They exist so completely outside the scope of such things that the Supernal simply cannot deal with them.<br /> <br /> As has been said above, the &quot;weirdness&quot;, &quot;otherness&quot;, and &quot;WTF-ness&quot; is part of the game and anything to ratchet that up is only a positive to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-20T15:14:32-07:00","id":143906,"title":"","content":"I like that idea - that there's no Supernal version of the Created.<br /> Remember that Mage cosmology <i>does not trump</i> Promethean cosmology (like, I mean, sure it does in a game where it does, but RAW? It's all just a toolkit and nothing is innately superior); if everything has a Supernal image, well hey! It's totally o-k that Prometheans break that rule.<br /> <br /> Imagine the look on the other player's faces if, when they find out you're a Promethean, they scan you and just get back a flat &quot;Nope&quot; for both Life and Death, and then &quot;Fucked If I Know&quot; for Prime.<br /> Bonus points if you make an Ulgan, so they can scan you with Spirit and get back a double negative. &quot;Not Entirely Unlike.&quot;<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1S8EuNtxeJKwq4sKVVPe16_N0ylIashKpgfCCuA1UOM8/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Promethean Homebrew.</a><br /> <br /> Yes, I made it the same way as a Promethean. No, the authorities haven't found me yet.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/685-ben-quo","name":"Ben Quo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar685_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-20T15:42:14-07:00","id":143922,"title":"","content":"Still think Forces would notice the Pyros fueling them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-20T18:37:18-07:00","id":144005,"title":"","content":"My preferred take is that the Principle and Pyros come from outside Mage\u2019s Supernal/Phenomenal dynamic entirely. Others have suggested the Lower Depths as its origin (a world that Mage describes as being to the Fallen World as the Fallen is to the Supernal); were I to try to tie Prometheans into Mage\u2019s cosmology, I\u2019d go the other way:<div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>The Empyrean</b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Courier New\">Confronted with a mutable Supernal, archmasters postulate that there must be an eternal, immutable causal plane beyond it: a Heaven, Nirvana, or Principle that fuels the Supernal with raw, undifferentiated meaning. Conservatives say that such a theory is unnecessary, given that the Supernal cannot be accurately perceived by any means short of Ascension, and may be truly pure under some veil of illusion. It is even said that some paths to Ascension bypass the Supernal and bring mages in accord with this true World Above \u2014 an idea Seekers invested in the Golden Road treat with disdain or curiosity.</span><br /> \u2014 <b>Imperial Mysteries</b>, page 53</div>This is another \u201coff the edge of the map\u201d thing, where mages (or, in this case, archmasters) are giving a name to something and then pretending that this means that they understand it: \u201cthe Lower Depths are to the Fallen World as the Fallen World is to the Supernal World; and the Empyrean is to the Supernal World as the Supernal World is to the Fallen World\u201d \u2014 whatever <i>that</i> means. Heck, archmasters aren\u2019t even in agreement as to whether or not the Empyrean <i>exists</i>; in practice, the term is effectively shorthand for \u201csomething that\u2019s not Supernal, Abyssal, Phenomenal/Fallen, or even of the mostly unknown Lower Depths\u201d.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 05-20-2014, 09:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-20T22:18:32-07:00","id":144175,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/116314-prometheans-are-what-exactly?p=144005#post144005\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My preferred take is that the Principle and Pyros come from outside Mage\u2019s Supernal/Phenomenal dynamic entirely. Others have suggested the Lower Depths as its origin (a world that Mage describes as being to the Fallen World as the Fallen is to the Supernal); were I to try to tie Prometheans into Mage\u2019s cosmology, I\u2019d go the other way:<div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>The Empyrean</b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Courier New\">Confronted with a mutable Supernal, archmasters postulate that there must be an eternal, immutable causal plane beyond it: a Heaven, Nirvana, or Principle that fuels the Supernal with raw, undifferentiated meaning. Conservatives say that such a theory is unnecessary, given that the Supernal cannot be accurately perceived by any means short of Ascension, and may be truly pure under some veil of illusion. It is even said that some paths to Ascension bypass the Supernal and bring mages in accord with this true World Above \u2014 an idea Seekers invested in the Golden Road treat with disdain or curiosity.</span><br /> \u2014 <b>Imperial Mysteries</b>, page 53</div>This is another \u201coff the edge of the map\u201d thing, where mages (or, in this case, archmasters) are giving a name to something and then pretending that this means that they understand it: \u201cthe Lower Depths are to the Fallen World as the Fallen World is to the Supernal World; and the Empyrean is to the Supernal World as the Supernal World is to the Fallen World\u201d \u2014 whatever <i>that</i> means. Heck, archmasters aren\u2019t even in agreement as to whether or not the Empyrean <i>exists</i>; in practice, the term is effectively shorthand for \u201csomething that\u2019s not Supernal, Abyssal, Phenomenal/Fallen, or even of the mostly unknown Lower Depths\u201d.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Whoever suggested The Lower Depths must not have read Promethean: The Created. Pyros and Azoth is described as pure adulterated force of inspiration, creation and brilliance. Something is fundamentally vibrant, that even to leave it just laying around will cause spontaneous creation of something, be it a storm of fire or a bunny. Azoth can spark life, animation and sentience back into dead flesh something that (to my knowledge anyway) the Life and Death Arcana, even combined, cannot truely do. If we look at the things thats been confirmed to be connected to The Lower Depths, we're dealing with things like The Decay from summoners, a being whose very pressence crumbles the world around it to dust, and who you feel on an instinctual level is just <i>wrong. </i><br /> We also have the sinful, cruel and selfish demons from Inferno, which i hardly think requires reasoning why they are bad candidates for Azoth-things.<br /> <br /> I could understand why you'de have come to that conclusion about Flux though. And in my opinion, that would make a cool contrast, with Azoth being the sorta &quot;Ultimate source of Good-Creation-Brightness energy&quot; and Flux being the sorta &quot;Ultimate source of Bad-Destruction-Darkness energy&quot;. Then Azoth would ebb from the sorta Supernal.^2 World, where as Flux would ebb from the sorta Lower.^2 Depths. That would put the &quot;Fallen&quot; World in a curious middle ground, where the forceses of Good and Bad are balanced inherently, and only our own choises define wich one takes hold pressently, which again would play into Prometheans main themes of philosophy and &quot;Blah-Blah-We-All-Know-This-Song&quot;.<br /> <br /> Generally, I am actually against pinning any definitive conclusions on the nature of Azoth and Flux. I think a good deal of their punch is that they're so mystical, and so powerful, and that the Prometheans dont really care about how powerful or mystical it is. To them, its just the force thats going to make them human once again, and liberate them from their tormentet existance. Thats all they need to know.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1958-krobeles","name":"Krobeles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1958_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-20T23:00:34-07:00","id":144204,"title":"","content":"First off, I would recommend abandoning the notion that Supernal-Fallen-Depths form a moral hierarchy; they don\u2019t. An ongoing argument that DaveB has been making is that the Supernal and Phenomenal are two interdependant halves of a whole, that neither could meaningfully exist without the other, and that neither is fundamentally \u201cbetter\u201d than the other. <br /> <br /> Second, Flux <i>is</i> Pyros; though Pyros is only sometimes Flux. What Flux contrasts with is Elpis. And Elpis/Flux isn\u2019t always a good/bad distinction, either: <b>Pandora\u2019s Book</b> includes a Lilithim who frees a Promethean from torture at the hands of what amounts to Ashwood Abbey and then proceeds to punish the torturers; and Elpis arguably also includes \u201cimprovements\u201d with nasty unintended consequences.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-20T23:24:38-07:00","id":144217,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/116314-prometheans-are-what-exactly?p=144204#post144204\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First off, I would recommend abandoning the notion that Supernal-Fallen-Depths form a moral hierarchy; they don\u2019t. An ongoing argument that DaveB has been making is that the Supernal and Phenomenal are two interdependant halves of a whole, that neither could meaningfully exist without the other, and that neither is fundamentally \u201cbetter\u201d than the other.<br /> <br /> Second, Flux <i>is</i> Pyros; though Pyros is only sometimes Flux. What Flux contrasts with is Elpis. And Elpis/Flux isn\u2019t always a good/bad distinction, either: <b>Pandora\u2019s Book</b> includes a Lilithim who frees a Promethean from torture at the hands of what amounts to Ashwood Abbey and then proceeds to punish the torturers; and Elpis arguably also includes \u201cimprovements\u201d with nasty unintended consequences.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well, yes. They do. To a certain extend anyway. The Demons of Inferno are from the Lower Depths, and they're inherently sinful and selfish. Of course Pyros in and of itself isn't a force of good, as I might've alluded to in my first post, but to say that the entirety of the Supernal/Fallen/Depths is entirely removed from a moral hierachy is just as wrong. I dont know what this Phenomenal is. What book is it from?<br /> <br /> Elpis is the force of hope, far as I remember. Flux is a force of dissolution and change. I wouldn't say they nessesarily contrast. Its a long time since I've read through it all, so that one is alittle hazy.<br /> From what I do think I remember though, is the fact that the Lillithim are pretty much always cruel, evil and disruptive. If the Lillithim set the Promethean free from the Ashwood Abby, it did so to facillitate some greater carnage somewhere else, someplace else. It might not even have anything to do with the Promethean in question directly. Though his freedom ensures, through some strange means, that a greater evil wil occur somewhere. And if the Lillithim 'punished' the Abby, it did so out of a sense of boredom and malice, more than a genuine sense that what they had done were wrong.<br /> Thats how I remember reading it, anyway. Might be wrong. Its been a while <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1958-krobeles","name":"Krobeles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1958_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-21T00:33:24-07:00","id":144237,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Krobeles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/116314-prometheans-are-what-exactly?p=144217#post144217\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, yes. They do. To a certain extend anyway. The Demons of Inferno are from the Lower Depths, and they're inherently sinful and selfish. Of course Pyros in and of itself isn't a force of good, as I might've alluded to in my first post, but to say that the entirety of the Supernal/Fallen/Depths is entirely removed from a moral hierachy is just as wrong. I dont know what this Phenomenal is. What book is it from?</div> </div> </div> </div><b>Imperial Mysteries</b>. It\u2019s a less disparaging term for what is more commonly called the Fallen World. As for the demons of the Inferno: yes, they\u2019re inherently sinful and selfish. But that\u2019s arguably because the thing they\u2019re missing is morals. And the Inferno is merely a tiny corner of the Lower Depths: the common feature of all of its denizens is that they\u2019re lacking something that the Phenomenal World has, and that the only way to fill that void it to take what they\u2019re lacking from the Phenomenal.<br /> <br /> And besides, there are plenty of beings native to the Phenomenal World who are every bit as inherently sinful and selfish as the Inferno\u2019s demons. And the closest thing to an official answer about the \u201clocation\u201d of <b>Changeling</b>\u2019s Arcadia places it in a remote region of the Supernal World (<b>Imperial Mysteries</b> again; look up the Old Gods of Thistle); the Gentry are <i>not</i> what I\u2019d call pillars of morality. Indeed, Old Gods <i>in general</i> don\u2019t seem to have much in the way of moral superiority; nor do the Exarchs who deposed them. The only known regions of the Supernal that might safely be characterized as having or facilitating morally good character are the Watchtower Realms. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Krobeles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/116314-prometheans-are-what-exactly?p=144217#post144217\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Elpis is the force of hope, far as I remember. Flux is a force of dissolution and change. I wouldn't say they nessesarily contrast. Its a long time since I've read through it all, so that one is alittle hazy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pyros is an agent of change. Elpis is that aspect of Pyros that focuses on constructive change; Flux is that aspect of Pyros that focuses on destructive change.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Krobeles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/116314-prometheans-are-what-exactly?p=144217#post144217\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From what I do think I remember though, is the fact that the Lillithim are pretty much always cruel, evil and disruptive. If the Lillithim set the Promethean free from the Ashwood Abby, it did so to facillitate some greater carnage somewhere else, someplace else. It might not even have anything to do with the Promethean in question directly. Though his freedom ensures, through some strange means, that a greater evil wil occur somewhere. And if the Lillithim 'punished' the Abby, it did so out of a sense of boredom and malice, more than a genuine sense that what they had done were wrong.<br /> Thats how I remember reading it, anyway. Might be wrong. Its been a while <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>The incident was a riff off of <i>The Masque of the Red Death</i>. The Lilithim in question specifically interrupted the Promethean\u2019s torture, told him to leave (\u201cthis is no place for you\u201d, or something to that effect), waited for him to leave, and then cursed the torturers with a nasty illness. There\u2019s no indication as to what, if any, further ramifications the incident had (other than the fact that the symptoms of its curse didn\u2019t manifest right away), so you basically have to take it on faith whether or not it facilitated greater carnage somewhere else. And once you start down that line of argument, you can argue that <i>any</i> act is being done in the service of evil; you just have to trace its consequences far enough to find one that was bad, and then say that that was the <i>real</i> reason the Lilithim intervened.<br /> <br /> The Lilithim aren\u2019t evil; they\u2019re destroyers. And the Elpidim aren\u2019t good; they\u2019re messengers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 05-21-2014, 03:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-21T01:10:45-07:00","id":144285,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/116314-prometheans-are-what-exactly?p=144237#post144237\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Lilithim aren\u2019t evil; they\u2019re destroyers. And the Elpidim aren\u2019t good; they\u2019re messengers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Opposed to one bringing rains to dry lands, bringing unity to communities, etc while the other does the exact opposite.<br /> <br /> Granted it's hard to elaborate on the nature of The Principle when it's agents are most active around Prometheans and given the numbers are so low, it's rather unsurprising that there isn't any documentation at all. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-21T08:46:08-07:00","id":144510,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/116314-prometheans-are-what-exactly?p=143922#post143922\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Still think Forces would notice the P