Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-07T18:03:04-07:00","id":190981,"title":"","content":"And Vitae, and Mana!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-08T00:55:19-07:00","id":191209,"title":"","content":"Guys, your all correct to an extent.<br /> <br /> Remember that Pyros is based on real world alchemical principles, and those principles revolve around breaking down matter to it's basic form in order to understand the building blocks of the universe so that the practitioner could better understand how to improve himself/herself physically, mentally, and spiritual. In the Promethean: The Created core rulebook it's stated that Pyros is a naturally occurring force that informs all life and being, so hypothetically all forms of energy could contain a bit of Pyros. After all if a mortal souls could be made from raw Pyros then who knows what else it could create given enough refinement and time.<br /> <br /> As for the original question I'm in the camp that believes a Promethean would register as recognizable but different to the scrutiny of Mage Sight. If there's enough Pyros gathered together to bend the rules of the universe enough to bring life to a lifeless corpse then any form of Mage Sight should be as equally confusing and unsettling as any other observation made about the Created...hypothetically of course.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-10T22:28:34-07:00","id":194350,"title":"","content":"honestly, what bugs me most on Promethean stuff is their relation to the God Machine.<br /> <br /> * I mean, there's this huge possibility of Pyros coming from the Empyrean/The Principle which the Promethean serve. It is also hinted that the souls are formed there by what is hinted to be the God Machine. <br /> <br /> * If the Empyrean is on the &quot;supernal side&quot; of reality (Tellurian) but not part of the Supernal, and the God Machine is inherent to the Phenomenal World, what is the relation between all of these things?<br /> <br /> Does anyone dare make this connection?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Historian ~ <b><a href=\"http://www.nwodbrasil.wordpress.com\" target=\"_blank\">www.cronistasdastrevasbr.com</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>I currently ST a... </b>MtAW 2e campaign called &quot;Axis Mundi - Si Vis Pacem&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/250-yuukale","name":"Yuukale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar250_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"391"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-10T22:44:09-07:00","id":194357,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yuukale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/116314-prometheans-are-what-exactly?p=194350#post194350\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">honestly, what bugs me most on Promethean stuff is their relation to the God Machine.<br /> <br /> * I mean, there's this huge possibility of Pyros coming from the Empyrean/The Principle which the Promethean serve. It is also hinted that the souls are formed there by what is hinted to be the God Machine.<br /> <br /> * If the Empyrean is on the &quot;supernal side&quot; of reality (Tellurian) but not part of the Supernal, and the God Machine is inherent to the Phenomenal World, what is the relation between all of these things?<br /> <br /> Does anyone dare make this connection?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Principle is not the God-Machine. There's some implications that the God-Machine might be crudely trying to copy the Principle, but the two are otherwise wholly unrelated. Promethean has no ties to God-Machine material other than the phrase &quot;god-machine&quot; getting used in <i>Magnum Opus</i> at one point and <i>qashmallim</i> showing up in the Demon core book.<br /> <br /> Don't try to relate Mage cosmology to everything else; down that road lies only madness. That said, I could see a theory that the God-Machine is a Fallen attempt to imitate the Principle, which exists somewhere in the Supernal or beyond and acts as a source of new souls. One might even say that Prometheans are to the Principle as Covers are to the God-Machine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-10T22:44:11-07:00","id":194358,"title":"","content":"My pet theory: the Principle and the God-Machine are distinct things. If you look at Gnosticism, they have what amounts to a \u201ctwo gods\u201d theory: a Creator, who made the universe and exists outside of it, and a Demiurge, who took the universe and turned it into a prison. Per the Gnostic theory, the Demiurge sealed creation off from the Creator, and the Creator has been working tirelessly to loosen the Demiurge\u2019s stranglehold on creation ever since.<br /> <br /> That\u2019s the Principle and the God-Machine: the Principle is an inscrutible Creator who exists outside the universe and seeks to reduce the God-Machine\u2019s influence; and the God-Machine is a Demiurge who has dominion over the world. I <i>suspect</i> that the Prodigal Demiurge mentioned in <b>Magnum Opus</b> might be the God-Machine, except that I don\u2019t see the God-Machine being responsible for the Promethean Lineages. It might possibly be responsible for the Unfleshed, though \u2014 they seem to be more its style.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 07-11-2014, 02:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-10T22:51:01-07:00","id":194360,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/116314-prometheans-are-what-exactly?p=194358#post194358\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My pet theory: the Principle and the God-Machine are distinct things. If you look at Gnosticism, they have what amounts to a \u201ctwo gods\u201d theory: a Creator, who made the universe and exists outside of it, and a Demiurge, who took the universe and turned it into a prison. Per the Gnostic theory, the Demiurge sealed creation off from the Creator, and the Creator has been working tirelessly to loosen the Demiurge\u2019s stranglehold on creation ever since. That\u2019s the Principle and the God-Machine: the Principle is an inscrutible Creator who exists outside the universe and seeks to reduce the God-Machine\u2019s influence; and the God-Machine is a Demiurge who has dominion over the world. I <i>suspect</i> that the Prodigal Demiurge mentioned in <b>Magnum Opus</b> might be the God-Machine, except that I don\u2019t see the God-Machine being responsible for the Promethean Lineages. It might possibly be responsible for the Unfleshed, though \u2014 they seem to be more its style.</div> </div> </div> </div>Precisely. Demon bills itself as a tech<b>gnostic</b> game, and while the Machine is rather clearly a demiurge/false divinity, there's no true divine for it to be contrasted against. But given that <i>qashmallim </i>are included in the Demon core for no explained reason, it would seem that the developers are deliberately setting up that contrast between the Machine and the Principle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-10T22:58:46-07:00","id":194363,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/116314-prometheans-are-what-exactly?p=194357#post194357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don't try to relate Mage cosmology to everything else; down that road lies only madness. That said, I could see a theory that the God-Machine is a Fallen attempt to imitate the Principle, which exists somewhere in the Supernal or beyond and acts as a source of new souls. One might even say that Prometheans are to the Principle as Covers are to the God-Machine.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh. I don\u2019t see a problem with incorporating <b>Imperial Mysteries</b>\u2019 speculation about the Empyrean and the God-Machine (yes, it has a blink-and-you-miss-it reference to the God-Machine) into this discussion. I think the pendulum may have swung too far the other way now, from what was once a tendency to try to cram everything into <b>Mage</b>\u2019s cosmology to a tendency these days to try to assert that <b>Mage</b>\u2019s cosmology is utterly meaningless outside of <b>Mage</b>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/116314-prometheans-are-what-exactly?p=194360#post194360\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Precisely. Demon bills itself as a tech<b>gnostic</b> game, and while the Machine is rather clearly a demiurge/false divinity, there's no true divine for it to be contrasted against. But given that <i>qashmallim </i>are included in the Demon core for no explained reason, it would seem that the developers are deliberately setting up that contrast between the Machine and the Principle.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-11T10:37:37-07:00","id":194769,"title":"","content":"I wholeheartedly thank you Data, for this connection. I do agree with your explanation and I will have it in mind when giving my opinion on these matters. Actually, I'll go and read a bit on gnosticism as well. Once more, thanks, I feel kinda happy (I think I got myself some arcane experience points).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Historian ~ <b><a href=\"http://www.nwodbrasil.wordpress.com\" target=\"_blank\">www.cronistasdastrevasbr.com</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>I currently ST a... </b>MtAW 2e campaign called &quot;Axis Mundi - Si Vis Pacem&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/250-yuukale","name":"Yuukale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar250_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"391"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-11T10:44:46-07:00","id":194778,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/116314-prometheans-are-what-exactly?p=194357#post194357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Principle is not the God-Machine. There's some implications that the God-Machine might be crudely trying to copy the Principle, but the two are otherwise wholly unrelated. Promethean has no ties to God-Machine material other than the phrase &quot;god-machine&quot; getting used in <i>Magnum Opus</i> at one point and <i>qashmallim</i> showing up in the Demon core book.</div> </div> </div> </div>... that we <i>know</i> of. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/116314-prometheans-are-what-exactly?p=194363#post194363\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eh. I don\u2019t see a problem with incorporating <b>Imperial Mysteries</b>\u2019 speculation about the Empyrean and the God-Machine (yes, it has a blink-and-you-miss-it reference to the God-Machine) into this discussion.</div> </div> </div> </div>Now that, I really liked. A very different perspective on the whole thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":877,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/877-mugasofer","user":"MugaSofer","date":". 07-11-2014, 01:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/877-mugasofer","name":"MugaSofer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar877_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-11T11:32:27-07:00","id":194814,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/116314-prometheans-are-what-exactly?p=194363#post194363\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eh. I don\u2019t see a problem with incorporating <b>Imperial Mysteries</b>\u2019 speculation about the Empyrean and the God-Machine (yes, it has a blink-and-you-miss-it reference to the God-Machine) into this discussion. I think the pendulum may have swung too far the other way now, from what was once a tendency to try to cram everything into <b>Mage</b>\u2019s cosmology to a tendency these days to try to assert that <b>Mage</b>\u2019s cosmology is utterly meaningless outside of <b>Mage</b>.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this is actually a good thing. On a surface level, one could say that its equally bad to devote ones entire attention to Mage, as it is to devote none to it, but atleast when we wholly neglect Mage's cosmology, we wont have to suffer the aggravating hordes of Mage fanatics going &quot;Your interpritation is WRONG! Allow me to qoute 7 paragraphs from [Insert obscure Mage expansion here], to prove how WRONG you are!&quot;.<br /> Ultimately, I think its all bloody pointless. We can debate back and forth what we feel is proper untill the sun explodes, and the best answer will still just be &quot;Do what works/is cooler in the context of your own scenario, not what the book says is 'the right way'.<br /> <br /> That said, I had an idea once, to interprid The Principle as The God-Machine of another reality. Perhaps let it be the God-Machine of the realm of ideas from old Greek Mythology. In this interpritation, The God-Machine of Demon is a strict system of laws and equations, matrices and infrastructure, because our reality is a physical one, ruled by strict laws and equations, matrices and infrastructure. The Principle on the other hand, being the ultimate force of governance of the Idea-World, is a much more fluid thing which humankind can only acess in short burts of inspiration or possibly upon death. This plays heavily into the old Greek philosophy of what an idea is, and the Idea-World is taken directly from Plato, I think it was.<br /> In this regard, Prometheans could almost be viewed as being half-ideas themselves, being dead flesh, sparked to unnatural (By the physical definition anyway) life by the sheer brightness of the idea that the Demiurge had of the ideal man, whom he wished to create, but useing physical and inert matter to do, didn't quite turn out to what he envisioned.<br /> Demons then, would be the former instruments of this physical worlds order, who had through some glitch in the divine code, attained the abillity to think and dream their own thoughts, possibly even to tap into the Idea-World to do so.<br /> Its not something I devoted overly much attention to, and it probably falls alittle flat, on account of basing everything I know about Demon off of the Quick-Start of Demon. But If i were to ever run a Demon-Promethean crossover, this would probably be how I'd do it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1958-krobeles","name":"Krobeles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1958_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-11T12:40:12-07:00","id":194911,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Krobeles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/116314-prometheans-are-what-exactly?p=194814#post194814\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think this is actually a good thing. On a surface level, one could say that its equally bad to devote ones entire attention to Mage, as it is to devote none to it, but atleast when we wholly neglect Mage's cosmology, we wont have to suffer the aggravating hordes of Mage fanatics going &quot;Your interpritation is WRONG! Allow me to qoute 7 paragraphs from [Insert obscure Mage expansion here], to prove how WRONG you are!&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh; I don\u2019t think the developers should be making game design decisions based off of horribly offensive stereotypes of <b>Mage</b> fans. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Krobeles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/116314-prometheans-are-what-exactly?p=194814#post194814\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ultimately, I think its all bloody pointless. We can debate back and forth what we feel is proper untill the sun explodes, and the best answer will still just be &quot;Do what works/is cooler in the context of your own scenario, not what the book says is 'the right way'.</div> </div> </div> </div><i>This,</i> I agree with. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-11T15:02:15-07:00","id":195021,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/116314-prometheans-are-what-exactly?p=194911#post194911\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eh; I don\u2019t think the developers should be making game design decisions based off of horribly offensive stereotypes of <b>Mage</b> fans.<br /> <br /> <i>This,</i> I agree with.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Developers? I wasn't talking about the developers. I'm not under the impression that they tried to cater to the Mage cosmology, nor am I under the impression that they cater less now than they used to. Sorry if I stereotyped the Mage fans. I dont know if I'm just unlucky, but I've seen some people being alittle too hyped on Mage to the exclusion and possible ostracization of the other game-lines. I meant no offense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1958-krobeles","name":"Krobeles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1958_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-11T19:29:42-07:00","id":195199,"title":"","content":"I dare say that while other games' cosmology is useful to better comprehend Mage's cosmology, the contrary isn't true.<br /> I mean, Promethean STs need not to take into account the other games or supernaturals (and whatever luggage they carry).<br /> Let Mage players try to link all, it is one of the points of their game. Promethean/Vampire/Werewolf/Etc aren't about understanding it all about the world, so they need not worry about this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Historian ~ <b><a href=\"http://www.nwodbrasil.wordpress.com\" target=\"_blank\">www.cronistasdastrevasbr.com</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>I currently ST a... </b>MtAW 2e campaign called &quot;Axis Mundi - Si Vis Pacem&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/250-yuukale","name":"Yuukale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar250_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"391"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-12T15:32:37-07:00","id":195799,"title":"","content":"When I run Mage I always have Prometheans as being understandable by the Supernal, because Mage cosmology is based around the Supernal being the &quot;absolute real&quot; and the Phenomenal being the &quot;context,&quot; which means Prometheans are the context of some sort of Supernal truth. I had to work quite hard for my players to really get how Mage works, in that way, and I wasn't too happy with everything and their dog then saying &quot;ooooh Mages don't get <i>this.&quot; </i>Well no, they don't yet, but they can find out.<br /> <br /> Of course, if I every ran Promethean, which I would like to do, I'd run it so that Prometheans are outside of Mage's cosmology. Then if they do come across a Mage they can be all &quot;I AM BEYOND YOUR COMPREHENSION&quot; because that's cool. It depends what the players are playing as.<br /> <br /> This does come back to me thinking that actually Mage probably works best when it's actually divorced from the other lines. Oh elements might come in (The Aegis Kai Doru, for example), but Mages don't really play well, what with their all encompassing cosmology and inherent drive to stick their noses into the most interesting mystery around and find out what it does. Mage doesn't benefit from the constant placing of stuff outside the Supernal and other splats don't really benefit from that. The","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/117-solar","name":"Solar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-12T17:53:30-07:00","id":195863,"title":"","content":"Eh; I see no more conflict between Mage nosiness and other supernaturals\u2019 themes than any given pair of supernaturals would have. Really, the Mage rep is one that it inherited from Ascension, where the premise of the game was (in grossly oversimplified terms) \u201cthe world works the way I say it does\u201d. With Awakening\u2019s focus on Mysteries, I could <i>easily</i> see mixing mages and non-mages in a single troupe, conceptually. <br /> <br /> As far as mixing Prometheans into a Mage game, I\u2019d <i>still</i> have them violate the core assumptions of Mage \u2014 or at least <i>seem</i> to. Not out of some one-upmanship, but because it poses questions and challenges assumptions. That said, there are still at least four conclusions a mage might come to concerning Prometheans:<br /> <br /> \u2022 The Pyros that animates them comes from the Supernal; but it comes from a part of the Supernal that\u2019s far from the known Watchtowers. <br /> \u2022 Pyros is an Abyssal energy. That\u2019s why you get Disquiet and Wastelands. <br /> \u2022 Pyros comes from the Lower Depths. After all, Prometheans are lacking something that people on Earth have, and they\u2019re desparately trying to get it. <br /> \u2022 Pyros is of the Empyrean. Note that because the Empyrean is strictly hypothetical as far as mages are concerned, this amounts to saying \u201cWe don\u2019t know where Pyros comes from or how it works\u201d \u2014 just dressed up with a fancy title. <br /> <br /> <b>Promethean</b>\u2019s phenomena present an \u201coutside context\u201d problem for mages; and that does great things for both <b>Mage</b> and <b>Promethean</b>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-12T17:55:46-07:00","id":195864,"title":"","content":"I actually think the prospect of a Promethean being incomprehensible to Mage's (atleast at the Mages current level of magical aptitude could work very well for the Mage.<br /> Sorta like a &quot;A new frontier awaits you!&quot; kinda thing. Like the cryo-sleep at end of every Sci-Fi movie/novel that screams &quot;And the Adventure continues!&quot;.<br /> It would also pose the question of what to do with this strange creature. Obviously, the Promethean will care jack-shit about being examined by the Mage, so does he try to force it to stay so he can study it? Lie to it, to compel it to stay? Make some deal and indept himself to its service at a later time, in return for the arcane knowledge that careful study might entail?<br /> <br /> I think you're needlessly deflating what could be a very cool plot-point by just going &quot;Yep. You can sorta understand this&quot;. Of course in the context of a Mage-centered chronicle, the Mage should be able to eventually come to some understanding of Pyros, if not direct control. But I feel like that should be true for any game, really. Its a staple of a bad story teller if he just goes &quot;Yeah, no! Out of bounds. Off limits. You'll never understand this, so you might as well stop trying&quot;. There are much more interesting stories and drama to be had, if you really hammer into the Mage, that he can only peripherally percieve this strange new energy, even with his all-mighty Prime Magesight.<br /> For a near omnipotent being who can resculpture reality with a though and a gesture, to be told that; &quot;Here you have a wierd man, held together by a powerful magical energy, which you dont understand, cant really percieve effectively, and worst of all, the man dosen't seem to give a shit about it!&quot; must be unthinkably infuriating. He could easily percieve it as a personal insult, on no fault of the Promethean, yet the Mage might not care. His all-knowingness has just had its toes stepped on, by a hobo in filthy rags! Thats the kind of thing that could make even a usually peachful Master fly into a frenzy.<br /> <br /> To actually throw a few thoughts to the original question:<br /> <br /> To sum it up, it basically comes down to the individual Promethean.<br /> <b>Dead:</b> If the Promethean has died at somepoint (like most Prometheans has) he'll ping the Death Magesight. Although some Prometheans (Like the Unfleshed) never died, and so they wont ping it.<br /> <b>Alive:</b> I would say most, if not all, Prometheans ping Life Magesight as being alive, to a certain extend. Even the Unfleshed are animated by the Divine Fire, and so they're alive up to a point.<br /> <b>Young/Old:</b> Depends on what you're useing to detect it. Most Death and Life spells check for the age of the body its being used on, and those will ping the aproximate age of the body.If you somehow engeneered some wierd spell (Perhaps something like Mind XX and Time XX?) and checked for the age of the individual's mind, you'd get the age of the Promethean has he appears before you, which could also be called the Actual age of the Promethean.<br /> <b>Forces: </b>A Promethean dosen't have an inherent electrical current or actual fire burning in his chest. What he has is a spiritual and metaphysical fire. Unless the Promethean has recently recharged himself with electricity or is useing a Transmutation that generates some strange energy fluctuations, I wouldn't say that Forces yields you anything too out of the ordinary. Perhaps an oddly low or high body temperature? Of course this sometimes ring false. A Nuclear Promethean will ping it like he is smeared with radioactive material, and an Unfleshed will probably register as having unnaturally powerful electrical currents running through his nervous system.<br /> <b>Prime:</b> This one is interesting. Although a Mage cannot actually percieve Pyros or Azoth itself, much less command it, he can percieve its effects and afterglow, much like a physicist would detect a virtual particle. This is probably a Mages best bet when dealing with a Promethean, as it can instantly see the firery glow radiating from a Prometheans pattern. Far as I remember, Prime is also required for the Legacy that actually lets you fuck about with Azoth and Pyros to the extend that a Mage can hope to, so if you want to fuck with Pyros and Azoth, Prime is your best buddie.<br /> <br /> <b>Additional Thoughts:</b><br /> Some Prometheans have been ripped apart by Spirits (And I see no reason why this notion could not be extended to Ghosts/Geists as well) and such a being will register heavily on a Spirit Magesight aswell. This is only one particular type of Promethean, but its worth mentioning. Additionally, the aformentioned Unfleshed, would probably ping Matter Magesight to a limited degree, due to their mechanical nature. Some rare few Prometheans are one-of-a-kind monsters, like this dude named Ben-Giera or something, who is compleately and entirely immortal so long as he remains on land (Not drowned in the ocean). Such a monster might ping some Magesight (Dont know which. Matter/Spirit/Death?) to show his connection to the undying and unyielding earth.<br /> Which again returns us to &quot;Its a case-by-case basis&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1958-krobeles","name":"Krobeles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1958_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-13T04:19:23-07:00","id":196183,"title":"","content":"I just think it's silly that Pyros and Azoth are outside of the ten Arcanum that cover everything else that exists. It might not be one-upmanship but it kind of feels like it. Mage cosmology is important to Mage, so in Mage it gets to stay constant and Pyros/Azoth are just weird forms of Prime, probably abyss tainted, that one can eventually learn to influence (although it may not be wise to do so, for it is still a mysterious and rarely seen substance). In Promethean, it can be outside of a Mage's purview because this is a Promethean game, not a Mage game, and Prometheans get their own way. But I like the fact that the Supernal is the Ultimate Truth of Everything. It gives it that weight which drives the Mage to catch glimpses of it from the corner of their eye... and that's lost if you say &quot;well it's the Ultimate Truth of Everything except this.&quot; A problem can and often should be outside of <i>a</i> Mage's context, but in the games I run it'll always be something that the Mage can learn about, because their purview is the Supernal and the Supernal twins with the Phenomenal to cover all.<br /> <br /> So should a Promethean come into my Mage game, it'll be visible through Prime Magesight in a similar, though not the same way, as a Tulpa might. A created being empowered by Aethyric forces which are in this case notably strange for sure, and why do they surge and flow so disconcertingly? Mind they definitely ping off, because they have a mind and are thinking beings. Life and Death also get pings, but in each case it's a weak signal, as if it is always being partially blocked. Through Life and Death at the same time, you get a full signal, but there's nothing like it you've ever seen. A Mage with Life, Death, Prime, Forces and Mind sees the whole deal and it's weird, whatever the hell it is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/117-solar","name":"Solar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-13T06:28:56-07:00","id":196230,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/116314-prometheans-are-what-exactly?p=196183#post196183\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just think it's silly that Pyros and Azoth are outside of the ten Arcanum that cover everything else that exists. It might not be one-upmanship but it kind of feels like it. Mage cosmology is important to Mage, so in Mage it gets to stay constant and Pyros/Azoth are just weird forms of Prime, probably abyss tainted, that one can eventually learn to influence (although it may not be wise to do so, for it is still a mysterious and rarely seen substance). In Promethean, it can be outside of a Mage's purview because this is a Promethean game, not a Mage game, and Prometheans get their own way. But I like the fact that the Supernal is the Ultimate Truth of Everything. It gives it that weight which drives the Mage to catch glimpses of it from the corner of their eye... and that's lost if you say &quot;well it's the Ultimate Truth of Everything except this.&quot; A problem can and often should be outside of <i>a</i> Mage's context, but in the games I run it'll always be something that the Mage can learn about, because their purview is the Supernal and the Supernal twins with the Phenomenal to cover all.</div> </div> </div> </div>I once heard somebody mention a realm that is to the Supernal as the Supernal is the Fallen. Called something like The Empyrion or something. Why not have Pyros and Azoth come from there? It would still baffle the fuck out of a regular Mage, giving that &quot;Oh noo! Its outside of my cosmology!&quot; feeling, while not actully being so. To an Archmaster, it would be vaguely undersandble, as is mentioned in the Prometheans books that it should be. This way you stay true to both systems, giving Pyros that mysterious and all-powerful feel that it needs to have, while still giving Mage a window to understand it.<br /> But ultimately, I honestly dont think staying true to the systems, and much less the fluff, of a splat is very important when that splat is only used as an NPC. I'll probably use some kind of Promethean in my Geist quest eventually, and I dont even plan on bringing Azoth or Pyros into the mix.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1958-krobeles","name":"Krobeles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1958_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-13T10:46:50-07:00","id":196426,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Krobeles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/116314-prometheans-are-what-exactly?p=196230#post196230\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I once heard somebody mention a realm that is to the Supernal as the Supernal is the Fallen. Called something like The Empyrion or something. Why not have Pyros and Azoth come from there? It would still baffle the fuck out of a regular Mage, giving that &quot;Oh noo! Its outside of my cosmology!&quot; feeling, while not actully being so. To an Archmaster, it would be vaguely undersandble, as is mentioned in the Prometheans books that it should be. This way you stay true to both systems, giving Pyros that mysterious and all-powerful feel that it needs to have, while still giving Mage a window to understand it.<br /> <br /> But ultimately, I honestly dont think staying true to the systems, and much less the fluff, of a splat is very important when that splat is only used as an NPC. I'll probably use some kind of Promethean in my Geist quest eventually, and I dont even plan on bringing Azoth or Pyros into the mix.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't mind that interpretation, to be honest. If Pyros/Azoth worked in a way which seemed to combine all of the Arcanum in a way that Mages don't understand, and was from above the Supernal, then you'd have the best of both. Investigation into this most rare and mysterious of supernatural beings would be the purview of only the wises and most knowledgeable Archmages, perhaps only the Ascended truly understand what forces lie beyond!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/117-solar","name":"Solar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-13T12:52:11-07:00","id":196527,"title":"","content":"It <i>was</i> one of the theories I proposed earlier \u2014 with the caveat that it\u2019s <i>just</i> a theory, in part because the <i>Empyrean</i> is just a theory: there is no confirmation, even among Archmasters, that it actually exists. You could point to Pyros as such evidence; but then you\u2019re getting into circular reasoning. <br /> <br /> A few pieces of <b>Mage</b> terminology \u2014 especially Empyrean and Lower Depths \u2014 are mage-speak for \u201cwe don\u2019t really know what this is.\u201d<br /> <br /> If the Storyteller decides that Pyros emanates directly from the Empyrean, he\u2019s free to so. I\u2019m not sure how that differs in practice from \u201cwe have no idea where it comes from\u201d, since the whole point of the Empyrean is that, if it exists, it\u2019s something that mages and archmasters can\u2019t really get a grip on, because it\u2019s outside their context. They\u2019re geared toward solving mysteries related to either the Supernal or the Fallen; anything from outside that context, such as the Abyss, the Lower Depths, or the Empyrean, gives them trouble.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-13T17:14:57-07:00","id":196608,"title":"","content":"The Abyss is kind of within Mage's purview in that it's an explicitly anti-Supernal force, and the Lower Depths are also within their purview in that it's kind of like a Fallen Fallen World, so it sits nicely within their cosmology. The Empryean is purely hypothetical in that it sits above the Supernal and nobody knows if it really exists, but I don't mind Pyros coming from there as it does kind of make sense (Pyros being this primal creative substance). The Principle as the ultimate truth, the Supernal as the facets of the Principle and so on. I don't mind filling in gaps to the system. I just don't like the idea that stuff exists outside the system entire as the whole point of a cosmology is that it does, in fact, set up the system of the cosmos. I feel that's a bit shitty for Mages as their cosmology is more important for them than Promethean cosmology is for Prometheans (which is a game with a far more personal focus).<br /> <br /> Though as I said, in a Mage game a Promethean is understandable and explainable by Mages, in a Promethean game it is not. I don't really like mixed splat parties so that conflict wouldn't come up for me, fortunately!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/117-solar","name":"Solar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-13T19:25:34-07:00","id":196640,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/116314-prometheans-are-what-exactly?p=196608#post196608\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Though as I said, in a Mage game a Promethean is understandable and explainable by Mages, in a Promethean game it is not. I don't really like mixed splat parties so that conflict wouldn't come up for me, fortunately!</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't nessesarily say a Promethean in a Promethean game should nessesarily be unexplainable. It just dosen't matter if it is or not, because the subject will likely never come up. If a Promethean, for whatever reason, chose to delve into it, I feel like he should have an equal shot at comming up with answers as a Mage should. Its ultimately still a mystery, even to the Prometheans themselves, but I feel like straight up negating the possibillity of having an answer exist, just because it isn't the main focus of the game, is doing yourself a major disservice.<br /> Roleplay is about having fun. And finding answers to questions your character has posed, is fun. The nature of Pyros and Azoth is a massively mysterious question, to be sure, but that'll only make it all the more gratyfing for the player when he finally finds an answer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1958-krobeles","name":"Krobeles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1958_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-14T06:10:28-07:00","id":196725,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Krobeles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/116314-prometheans-are-what-exactly?p=195864#post195864\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To sum it up, it basically comes down to the individual Promethean.<br /> <b>Dead:</b> If the Promethean has died at somepoint (like most Prometheans has) he'll ping the Death Magesight. Although some Prometheans (Like the Unfleshed) never died, and so they wont ping it.<br /> <b>Alive:</b> I would say most, if not all, Prometheans ping Life Magesight as being alive, to a certain extend. Even the Unfleshed are animated by the Divine Fire, and so they're alive up to a point.<br /> <b>Young/Old:</b> Depends on what you're useing to detect it. Most Death and Life spells check for the age of the body its being used on, and those will ping the aproximate age of the body.If you somehow engeneered some wierd spell (Perhaps something like Mind XX and Time XX?) and checked for the age of the individual's mind, you'd get the age of the Promethean has he appears before you, which could also be called the Actual age of the Promethean.<br /> <b>Forces: </b>A Promethean dosen't have an inherent electrical current or actual fire burning in his chest. What he has is a spiritual and metaphysical fire. Unless the Promethean has recently recharged himself with electricity or is useing a Transmutation that generates some strange energy fluctuations, I wouldn't say that Forces yields you anything too out of the ordinary. Perhaps an oddly low or high body temperature? Of course this sometimes ring false. A Nuclear Promethean will ping it like he is smeared with radioactive material, and an Unfleshed will probably register as having unnaturally powerful electrical currents running through his nervous system.<br /> <b>Prime:</b> This one is interesting. Although a Mage cannot actually percieve Pyros or Azoth itself, much less command it, he can percieve its effects and afterglow, much like a physicist would detect a virtual particle. This is probably a Mages best bet when dealing with a Promethean, as it can instantly see the firery glow radiating from a Prometheans pattern. Far as I remember, Prime is also required for the Legacy that actually lets you fuck about with Azoth and Pyros to the extend that a Mage can hope to, so if you want to fuck with Pyros and Azoth, Prime is your best buddie.<br /> <br /> <b>Additional Thoughts:</b><br /> Some Prometheans have been ripped apart by Spirits (And I see no reason why this notion could not be extended to Ghosts/Geists as well) and such a being will register heavily on a Spirit Magesight aswell. This is only one particular type of Promethean, but its worth mentioning. Additionally, the aformentioned Unfleshed, would probably ping Matter Magesight to a limited degree, due to their mechanical nature. Some rare few Prometheans are one-of-a-kind monsters, like this dude named Ben-Giera or something, who is compleately and entirely immortal so long as he remains on land (Not drowned in the ocean). Such a monster might ping some Magesight (Dont know which. Matter/Spirit/Death?) to show his connection to the undying and unyielding earth.<br /> Which again returns us to &quot;Its a case-by-case basis&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would only add that for:<br /> <br /> <b>Matter</b> - ALL Prometheans are &quot;things&quot;. When they are &quot;alive&quot; now, they started as inanimate pile of recourse - is it humans corpses, or technology, or even wood or marble. They are now &quot;alive inanimate&quot;, with human bodies also part of Matter preview.<br /> <br /> <b>Mind</b> - Obviously, Created have a Mind in Arcanum understanding, maybe twisted by Disquiet and not &quot;proper human&quot;. But should *ping* on Mind SIght also as being.<br /> <br /> <b>Spirit</b> - I would posit that they also are detectable by this Arcanum, as souls are, and Prometheans have &quot;proto-souls&quot;. They look weird but they are there.<br /> <br /> <b>Forces</b> - weird electric current of they bodies, and suitability for taking thunder on them should also be possible to study here.<br /> <br /> And finally, to the last one...<br /> <br /> <b>Fate</b> - here is Arcanum I think that <b>can't</b> study Created. Fate study Destiny, and Destiny is function of soul proper. Also, the Flux element in all Prometheans and they &quot;free will&quot; is disrupts this thing. <br /> <br /> I'm also is in favor of Principle=Emperyan theory, at least for Mysterium scholars in mages sociaety. I envison that Athenums Cultor seeing notes onf found Created would goes &quot;this must be from the world above the Supernal, OMG...&quot;<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-14T12:25:39-07:00","id":197090,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/116314-prometheans-are-what-exactly?p=196608#post196608\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Abyss is kind of within Mage's purview in that it's an explicitly anti-Supernal force, and the Lower Depths are also within their purview in that it's kind of like a Fallen Fallen World, so it sits nicely within their cosmology. The Empryean is purely hypothetical in that it sits above the Supernal and nobody knows if it really exists, but I don't mind Pyros coming from there as it does kind of make sense (Pyros being this primal creative substance). The Principle as the ultimate truth, the Supernal as the facets of the Principle and so on. I don't mind filling in gaps to the system. I just don't like the idea that stuff exists outside the system entire as the whole point of a cosmology is that it does, in fact, set up the system of the cosmos. I feel that's a bit shitty for Mages as their cosmology is more important for them than Promethean cosmology is for Prometheans (which is a game with a far more personal focus).</div> </div> </div> </div>Think of it this way: it\u2019s not that it doesn\u2019t fit; it\u2019s that it doesn\u2019t fit in the same way that everything else does: you can\u2019t point to certain Arcana that deal with Promethean phenomena the way you can for other greater templates. (It\u2019s worth noting that when <b>Imperial Mysteries</b> goes down the checklist of gameline templates and which Arcana are used to mess with them, it makes no mention of anything related to <b>Promethean</b>.) Setting aside the philosophical issues of whether or not mages can find a label that seems to fit, <i>this</i> is the important part: regardless of which explanation you use to fit Pyros into <b>Mage</b>\u2019s metaphysics, all things Pyros remain largely beyond the scope of Supernal Magic. <br /> <br /> \u2022 Pyros is covered by Supernal symbols that aren\u2019t anywhere near the Watchtowers. Since the Arcana that mages study are near the Watchtowers, that still leaves Pyros beyond their reach. <br /> \u2022 Pyros comes from the Abyss. Without delving into Abyssal Magic, Pyros is beyond a mage\u2019s reach. Even <i>with</i> Abyssal Magic, nobody has been able to figure out how to mess with Pyros. <br /> \u2022 Pyros comes from the Lower Depths. If this is true, then Pyros represents a void that the Arcana don\u2019t cover. <br /> \u2022 Pyros comes from the Empyrean. If <i>this</i> is true, then not even conjunctional use of all ten Arcana would be enough to cover Pyros. <br /> \u2022 Pyros is purely of the Phenomenal World, with no source beyond the Phenomenal. Then Supernal Magic has nothing that can cover it. <br /> <br /> Note that several of these options say things about <b>Mage</b>\u2019s metaphysics, such as pointing to the expansiveness of the Supernal or the possibility of a \u201ctrans-Supernal world\u201d, or even the possibility that the Supernal/Phenomenal interdependence isn\u2019t as absolute as mages tend to think. These are possibilities that enrich <b>Mage</b> in a way that \u201cPyros is a weird kind of Prime\u201d doesn\u2019t. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/116314-prometheans-are-what-exactly?p=196608#post196608\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Though as I said, in a Mage game a Promethean is understandable and explainable by Mages, in a Promethean game it is not. I don't really like mixed splat parties so that conflict wouldn't come up for me, fortunately!</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019m saying that whether or not it\u2019s understandable and explainable by mages is most likely to be important in a <b>Mage</b> game, not a <b>Promethean</b> game; and unless the Storyteller invokes his \u201cI can do whatever I want, no matter what the books say\u201d right, the answer <i>still</i> appears to be that Prometheans aren\u2019t explainable by mages, or even by archmasters. They can <i>hypothesize</i>; but Promethean metaphysics lie beyond the boundaries of even Mage metaphysics. <br /> <br /> Which simply means that <b>Mage</b> doesn\u2019t have a Theory of Everything. That\u2019s not a knock against <b>Mage: the Awakening</b>; unlike <b>Mage: the Ascension</b>, <b>Awakening</b> is more concerned with questions than with answers. The fact that there are questions that they don\u2019t have answers to \u2014 and might not even be properly equipped to answer \u2014 merely means that there\u2019s more work to be done. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-14T13:27:10-07:00","id":197131,"title":"","content":"And more fun to be had!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-14T14:48:57-07:00","id":197201,"title":"","content":"Anyway the real answer to this question is that Prometheans are shifty and suspicious and there's no place for them here <i>that's</i> for sure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/117-solar","name":"Solar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-14T14:52:37-07:00","id":197206,"title":"","content":"What, are you joking? Of course there is!<br /> <br /> Right down there, in my basement laboratory.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-14T15:01:10-07:00","id":197214,"title":"","content":"The only good Promethean is a dead Promethean<br /> <br /> er<br /> <br /> dead<i>er</i> Promethean<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/117-solar","name":"Solar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-14T15:02:44-07:00","id":197216,"title":"","content":"They are alive, after a fashion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-14T23:07:17-07:00","id":197583,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/116314-prometheans-are-what-exactly?p=197090#post197090\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019m saying that whether or not it\u2019s understandable and explainable by mages is most likely to be important in a <b>Mage</b> game, not a <b>Promethean</b> game; and unless the Storyteller invokes his \u201cI can do whatever I want, no matter what the books say\u201d right, the answer <i>still</i> appears to be that Prometheans aren\u2019t explainable by mages, or even by archmasters. They can <i>hypothesize</i>; but Promethean metaphysics lie beyond the boundaries of even Mage metaphysics.<br /> <br /> Which simply means that <b>Mage</b> doesn\u2019t have a Theory of Everything. That\u2019s not a knock against <b>Mage: the Awakening</b>; unlike <b>Mage: the Ascension</b>, <b>Awakening</b> is more concerned with questions than with answers. The fact that there are questions that they don\u2019t have answers to \u2014 and might not even be properly equipped to answer \u2014 merely means that there\u2019s more work to be done.</div> </div> </div> </div>And they are wellspring of Arcane Experience - really, I want just to play/run Mage-Promethan crossover just because all the Created is and doing are instant Mystery on itself, and whole thing with &quot;Mysterium want's it in their lab and Guardians want's it be dead&quot; is just too much fun and ready chronicle. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 07-15-2014, 04:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-15T06:53:27-07:00","id":197880,"title":"","content":"Being that I've started the process of rereading Promethean in its entirety from the core in the last few days I feel a pointed reminder is necessary about how Supernal magic works and why, thematically, the Pyros is thus tricky for mortal manipulations of the fundament to grasp:<br /> <br /> The Supernal World describes and acts upon the Phenomenal World. Take note of that first verb in particular \u2014 Awakening's made its share of references to magic's connection with language.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, I'm not even done with the first chapter of Promethean Core yet and already I've hit two or three references to the Pyros, the soul, and Azoth being indescribable mysteries.<br /> <br /> The fact that the Divine Fire is pervasive is kind of a hint that the supernatural mechanisms of human understanding that divide the cosmos into a double-handful of phenomenal constellations aren't the right equipment for the sort of holistic approach needed to grasp the stuff in more than the abstract sense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-15T23:51:17-07:00","id":198630,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/116314-prometheans-are-what-exactly?p=197880#post197880\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The fact that the Divine Fire is pervasive is kind of a hint that the supernatural mechanisms of human understanding that divide the cosmos into a double-handful of phenomenal constellations aren't the right equipment for the sort of holistic approach needed to grasp the stuff in more than the abstract sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>So they could get *ping* on particular Arcanum Sight, but nowhere to concept whole power of Pyros. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-16T02:52:02-07:00","id":198761,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/116314-prometheans-are-what-exactly?p=197880#post197880\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Being that I've started the process of rereading Promethean in its entirety from the core in the last few days I feel a pointed reminder is necessary about how Supernal magic works and why, thematically, the Pyros is thus tricky for mortal manipulations of the fundament to grasp:<br /> <br /> The Supernal World describes and acts upon the Phenomenal World. Take note of that first verb in particular \u2014 Awakening's made its share of references to magic's connection with language.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, I'm not even done with the first chapter of Promethean Core yet and already I've hit two or three references to the Pyros, the soul, and Azoth being indescribable mysteries.</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering Pyros has the ability to &quot;burn out&quot; Gnosis in the Awakened, I would consider it being able to &quot;burn out&quot; symbols in the Supernal (specifically names on Watchtowers). <br /> <br /> As Above, so Below and all that jazz.<br /> <br /> Which would be ironic is that was discovered by the Seers/Pentacle. A force that could in theory win the Ascension War that neither force can actually handle nor control without losing their ability to use magic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-16T05:45:32-07:00","id":198849,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shock</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/116314-prometheans-are-what-exactly?p=198761#post198761\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Considering Pyros has the ability to &quot;burn out&quot; Gnosis in the Awakened, I would consider it being able to &quot;burn out&quot; symbols in the Supernal (specifically names on Watchtowers).<br /> <br /> As Above, so Below and all that jazz.<br /> <br /> Which would be ironic is that was discovered by the Seers/Pentacle. A force that could in theory win the Ascension War that neither force can actually handle nor control without losing their ability to use magic.</div> </div> </div> </div>Burn out? Say what now? Where does it say that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1958-krobeles","name":"Krobeles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1958_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-16T10:48:24-07:00","id":199111,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Krobeles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/116314-prometheans-are-what-exactly?p=198849#post198849\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Burn out? Say what now? Where does it say that?</div> </div> </div> </div>Saturnine Night's section on supernatural demiurges. The stuff can <i>melt ideas</i>.<br /> <br /> &quot;Pyros heats all substances and even ideas, melting them into new shapes and inspirations. It is not just <i>form</i> that it alters; that is a lesser power, available throughout Nature. Pyros also alters <i>qualities</i>, turning one thing into something entirely other.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-16T12:04:40-07:00","id":199140,"title":"","content":"That's why the Pyros mutates stuff in 50s-esque radiation style.<br /> It's why you get permutations on the Lineages.<br /> It's why you can make a Galatead out of flesh or marble, and why you can <i>dream a Promethean into existence</i> (which, you know. Very tulpa-esque. Thought constructs and all that).<br /> <br /> What's important about Promethean isn't the answer; the answer is mortality, that or becoming a monster the likes of which the world has never known.<br /> What's important is <i>getting there.</i> The Pilgrimage. It's a mystery how you exist (as encompassed by the fact that a Demiurge's notes aren't going to make a whole lot of sense and are incredibly difficult to find; think about it: the best advice you have about your condition and how to make another like you is <i>barely accessible</i>). It's a mystery how you become human.<br /> <br /> Mage's solve Mysteries!<br /> They solve <i>their own</i> mysteries though.<br /> Socketing the one gameline that is, by design, supposed to be outside context for <i>every other character in the entire system</i> into &quot;Mage's can figure it out&quot; cheapens both gamelines.<br /> You don't need to have a Promethean in a chronicle to have a patchwork man in it. There's far richer story potential in &quot;he doesn't ping to your Magesight/you don't know&quot; than &quot;he's XYZ.&quot;<br /> <br /> Anyway, even if you <i>do</i> want Prometheans to be a solvable mystery in <i>your</i> Mage campaign (which is fine! It's yours twice now), wouldn't it be better for it to be something they can't figure out? Wouldn't it be better for them to have to take time to go explore it?<br /> <br /> Prometheans aren't human. Not yet. They aren't anything. This is why the game is cool - they don't know what kind of person they are yet. They aren't alive or dead or undead. They're making a soul.<br /> It's probably telling that the first thing a Mage has to do to actually learn about a Promethean is overcome Disquiet, and even <i>realizing</i> that such a thing is working upon them is a huge pain in the ass.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1S8EuNtxeJKwq4sKVVPe16_N0ylIashKpgfCCuA1UOM8/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Promethean Homebrew.</a><br /> <br /> Yes, I made it the same way as a Promethean. No, the authorities haven't found me yet.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/685-ben-quo","name":"Ben Quo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar685_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-16T14:56:40-07:00","id":199302,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shock</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/116314-prometheans-are-what-exactly?p=198761#post198761\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Considering Pyros has the ability to &quot;burn out&quot; Gnosis in the Awakened, I would consider it being able to &quot;burn out&quot; symbols in the Supernal (specifically names on Watchtowers).</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Krobeles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/116314-prometheans-are-what-exactly?p=198849#post198849\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Burn out? Say what now? Where does it say that?</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/116314-prometheans-are-what-exactly?p=199111#post199111\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Saturnine Night's section on supernatural demiurges. The stuff can <i>melt ideas</i>.<br /> <br /> &quot;Pyros heats all substances and even ideas, melting them into new shapes and inspirations. It is not just <i>form</i> that it alters; that is a lesser power, available throughout Nature. Pyros also alters <i>qualities</i>, turning one thing into something entirely other.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>This. Although the terminology that <b>Mage</b> uses isn\u2019t used here, that\u2019s what Supernal symbols <i>are</i>: the qualities of the Fallen World\u2019s Phenomena. And the whole purpose for setting it up like this is that mages <i>should</i> look at it and say \u201choly crap! What the hell is <i>that</i>?\u201d Not just \u201cI say, good sir, what is that strange thing you have going on there?\u201d. A visceral WTF moment rather than mere curiosity. Incidentally, that\u2019s also why mages aren\u2019t immune to Disquiet. <br /> <br /> <i>Maybe</i> an archmaster could use his Ascension to rewrite reality so that Pyros is a phenomenon emanating from the Aether. <i>Maybe</i>. (What happens when an unstoppable force meets an immovable object?) But aside from that, Pyros is an \u201coutside context\u201d problem that mages simply aren\u2019t equipped to handle. <br /> <br /> Shock\u2019s reference is that <b>Saturnine Night</b> says that a mage <i>can</i> create a Promethean \u2014 but only by <i>not</i> using magic and doing it the way regular mortals do; and even then, his Gnosis takes a hit and he risks losing his Mage template. (I wouldn\u2019t go <i>quite</i> as far as <b>Saturnine Night</b> does in that I\u2019d leave the poor wreck as a Sleepwalker rather than a Sleeper; whether or not he has a signature on a Watchtower, he\u2019s already broken free of the Sleeping Curse, and I don\u2019t see it reasserting itself even if his Watchtower connection gets burned out.)<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-16T16:45:45-07:00","id":199406,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/116314-prometheans-are-what-exactly?p=199302#post199302\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>Maybe</i> an archmaster could use his Ascension to rewrite reality so that Pyros is a phenomenon emanating from the Aether. <i>Maybe</i>. (What happens when an unstoppable force meets an immovable object?) But aside from that, Pyros is an \u201coutside context\u201d problem that mages simply aren\u2019t equipped to handle.</div> </div> </div> </div>An archmage doing that would imply that the Supernal has power over the Divine Fire which given current evidence leans to the belief that this is not the case.<br /> <br /> He is certainly welcome to try but his attempts would be frustrated at best.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-16T17:00:07-07:00","id":199420,"title":"","content":"There\u2019s a reason I said \u201c<i>maybe</i>\u201d. It <i>is</i> possible that Pyros has Supernal symbols associated with it, just not any that are associated with the Arcana. <i>If</i> that is true, then it might be possible for an Archmaster to use Imperium to alter those symbols. There are a lot of \u201cif\u201ds there; but they can\u2019t be ruled out conclusively.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-16T19:10:43-07:00","id":199548,"title":"","content":"Isn't pyros supposed to be the raw material of which the supernal is made of? Therefore, you can't change it through supernal manipulation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Historian ~ <b><a href=\"http://www.nwodbrasil.wordpress.com\" target=\"_blank\">www.cronistasdastrevasbr.com</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>I currently ST a... </b>MtAW 2e campaign called &quot;Axis Mundi - Si Vis Pacem&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/250-yuukale","name":"Yuukale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar250_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"391"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-16T19:12:55-07:00","id":199549,"title":"","content":"That\u2019s an interesting theory; but no. The closest you get to \u201craw stuff of the Supernal\u201d is Mana, not Pyros.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-16T19:21:35-07:00","id":199553,"title":"","content":"Well, according to the box on Imperial Mysteries this is a possibility:<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;confronted with a mutable Supernal, archmasters postulate that there must be an eternal, immutable causal plane beyond it: a Heaven, Nirvana, or Principle that fuels the Supernal with raw, undifferentiated meaning.</span></span></span>&quot; IM pg.53","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Historian ~ <b><a href=\"http://www.nwodbrasil.wordpress.com\" target=\"_blank\">www.cronistasdastrevasbr.com</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>I currently ST a... </b>MtAW 2e campaign called &quot;Axis Mundi - Si Vis Pacem&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/250-yuukale","name":"Yuukale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar250_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"391"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-16T19:53:37-07:00","id":199565,"title":"","content":"See <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/116314-prometheans-are-what-exactly?p=144005#post144005\">Post #20</a> for the full text.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-17T10:13:39-07:00","id":200178,"title":"","content":"well, that neither confirms nor denies this possibility, afaik. Given everything there is about Pyros and the Empyrean, I tend to think this is a nice approach. What more, with the whole creatorXdemiurge thing, it sounds even more plausible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Historian ~ <b><a href=\"http://www.nwodbrasil.wordpress.com\" target=\"_blank\">www.cronistasdastrevasbr.com</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>I currently ST a... </b>MtAW 2e campaign called &quot;Axis Mundi - Si Vis Pacem&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/250-yuukale","name":"Yuukale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar250_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"391"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-17T10:41:45-07:00","id":200239,"title":"","content":"So on a slightly more serious note than my last post: In my own head canon, I've long equated the Supernal with the concept of <i>fact</i> or <i>being</i>, and the Principle with the concept of <i>intent</i>. I also don't hold the Principle as &quot;above&quot; or &quot;fueling&quot; the Supernal in any way, one is the structure and the other is the blueprints.<br /> <br /> The Supernal's concept of <i>being</i> is the foundational aspects of existence that point in the direction it will go in; one cell divides into two at a time; cutting a human in half causes it to die; a single insect is incapable of the level of cognition of a human. The Principle's concept of <i>intent</i> is the movement in that direction, or the application of the aspect on that particular aspect of existence; why the cell divides in *that* direction, why it divides at all, and why it stops; why a human doesn't regrow lost limbs; that while one insect is incapable of higher cognition, a hivemind allows for more advanced and complex behaviors than the simplicity of the rules would seem to allow.<br /> <br /> Azoth, being the concentrated form of the Principle, changes this in the way of how the building would look if you built the blueprints in a different order, or randomly swapped aspects between blueprints; one cell could divide into three or four at a time, or lose its regulatory mechanism to <u>stop</u> dividing when it should; a human exhibits a starfish's or earthworm's fundamental <i>intent</i> of survival and growth, regrowing the missing half when split in half; an insect is able to force non-insect minds into its hivemind, increasing its cognitive abilities by orders of magnitude (okay, I just gave myself nightmares for the next month...)<br /> <br /> Prometheans are continuations of the effects that Azoth had on the blueprints of existence. Dead flesh reanimating. Stone sculptures stepping into the existence their forms mimic. Etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Once is happenstance. Twice is coincidence. Three times is enemy action. Four times is Infrastructure.<br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> Rule #2: Never let the game-mechanics get in the way of a good story.","edited":{"userid":1642,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1642-paddon","user":"Paddon","date":".  a word 07-18-2014, 12:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1642-paddon","name":"Paddon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1642_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"326"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-17T19:21:02-07:00","id":200656,"title":"","content":"\u2026and here\u2019s an example of an explanation for Pyros that\u2019s interesting but would be lost if \u201cPyros comes from the Empyrean\u201d was an established fact. I\u2019m not sure I\u2019d use Paddon\u2019s explanation myself (though it has a lot to recommend it); but I like having the option to do so. Without having to invoke Rule #1, that is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-17T23:36:48-07:00","id":200774,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yuukale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/116314-prometheans-are-what-exactly?p=194350#post194350\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">honestly, what bugs me most on Promethean stuff is their relation to the God Machine.<br /> <br /> * I mean, there's this huge possibility of Pyros coming from the Empyrean/The Principle which the Promethean serve. It is also hinted that the souls are formed there by what is hinted to be the God Machine.<br /> <br /> * If the Empyrean is on the &quot;supernal side&quot; of reality (Tellurian) but not part of the Supernal, and the God Machine is inherent to the Phenomenal World, what is the relation between all of these things?<br /> <br /> Does anyone dare make this connection?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's the Celestial Escalator. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T03:40:07-07:00","id":233988,"title":"","content":"So, I'm not sure if this was fully addressed in this thread, but Prometheans have a &quot;fiery aura&quot; to Prime Sight. Life and Death Sight can requires scrutiny before it figures out they're a Promethean (the scrutiny roll requires a number of successes equal to 10-Azoth). In addition, if the Promethean's disfigurements are ever revealed, then those two Sights automatically reveal the Promethean as a Promethean.<br /> <br /> Also of interest: apparently Prometheans show no sign of &quot;bring unnatural&quot;. This in reference to Mages maybe freaking out at weird, tainted souls screwing with &quot;actual souls&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/274-enokh","name":"Enokh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar274_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"474"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}